    "body": "Hi EgiGrivandani,\n\nWhich app did you notice was broken first once the cleanup finished?\n\nFreeing up disk space is about as ordinary a request as it gets, and the CapCut and Postman leftovers were sensible targets, yet one rmdir /s /q wrapped in cmd.exe with backslash escaped quotes was enough to send it walking through Program Files and your user folders. The 38,271 lines in task-327.log, with over 35,000 of them pointing at Program Files, tell the story better than any summary could. What bothers me most is that the only thing standing between that command and your drive was the same model that wrote it, and it had no reason to doubt its own quoting. A separate check that reads the final resolved path before any recursive delete runs, and refuses anything at a drive root or under Program Files or Windows, seems like the bare minimum for a request like this. Losing PowerShell with no restore point is a brutal way to find that gap, and keeping steps 326 and 327 around should help a lot when the team digs in.\n\nSam\n",
